<root class="learn">
  <header class="learn-head">
    <span class="dc-eyebrow">tutorial</span>
    <h1>Build a Todo app</h1>
    <p>
      A few small steps take you from an empty struct to a working,
      reactive Todo — the same one running on the right. No build step
      beyond <code>pocopine dev</code>, no virtual DOM, no JavaScript.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="learn-grid">
    <nav class="learn-nav" aria-label="Chapters">
      <a href="#s1" :data-active="active == 1 ? 'true' : 'false'"><span>1</span>The model</a>
      <a href="#s2" :data-active="active == 2 ? 'true' : 'false'"><span>2</span>The component</a>
      <a href="#s3" :data-active="active == 3 ? 'true' : 'false'"><span>3</span>Render the list</a>
      <a href="#s4" :data-active="active == 4 ? 'true' : 'false'"><span>4</span>Add a task</a>
      <a href="#s5" :data-active="active == 5 ? 'true' : 'false'"><span>5</span>Toggle &amp; remove</a>
      <a href="#s6" :data-active="active == 6 ? 'true' : 'false'"><span>6</span>Persist on the server</a>
      <a href="#s7" :data-active="active == 7 ? 'true' : 'false'"><span>7</span>Ship it</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="learn-main">
      <section id="s1" class="learn-sec" pp-intersect:enter.margin.0.0.-70%.0="enter1">
        <h2>The model</h2>
        <p>Start with the data. A todo is a plain Rust struct — an id, the text, and whether it's done. Deriving <code>Serialize</code> lets pocopine move it across the reactive boundary and the wire.</p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code pp-text="code1"></code></pre>
      </section>

      <section id="s2" class="learn-sec" pp-intersect:enter.margin.0.0.-70%.0="enter2">
        <h2>The component</h2>
        <p>A component is a struct plus a sibling <code>.poco</code> template. State is just fields: the list of todos and the text being typed. No stores, no <code>Rc&lt;RefCell&gt;</code> — pocopine makes the fields reactive for you.</p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code pp-text="code2"></code></pre>
      </section>

      <section id="s3" class="learn-sec" pp-intersect:enter.margin.0.0.-70%.0="enter3">
        <h2>Render the list</h2>
        <p>The template is HTML with directives. <code>pp-for</code> repeats a <code>&lt;template&gt;</code> for each item, <code>pp-text</code> binds the label, and a bound <code>:data-done</code> attribute lets CSS strike through finished tasks.</p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code pp-text="code3"></code></pre>
      </section>

      <section id="s4" class="learn-sec" pp-intersect:enter.margin.0.0.-70%.0="enter4">
        <h2>Add a task</h2>
        <p>An input bound with <code>pp-model</code> keeps <code>draft</code> in sync. The form's submit handler pushes a new todo and clears the field — and the list re-renders automatically. Try it in the preview.</p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code pp-text="code4"></code></pre>
      </section>

      <section id="s5" class="learn-sec" pp-intersect:enter.margin.0.0.-70%.0="enter5">
        <h2>Toggle &amp; remove</h2>
        <p>One click handler on the list reads which item was clicked and flips or removes it. Mutate the field; the view follows. That's the whole interaction model.</p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code pp-text="code5"></code></pre>
      </section>

      <section id="s6" class="learn-sec" pp-intersect:enter.margin.0.0.-70%.0="enter6">
        <h2>Persist on the server</h2>
        <p>Mark a function <code>#[server]</code> and it compiles to a real backend route plus a typed client stub. Call it from the browser like any async function — same language, same types, both ends.</p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code pp-text="code6"></code></pre>
      </section>

      <section id="s7" class="learn-sec" pp-intersect:enter.margin.0.0.-70%.0="enter7">
        <h2>Ship it</h2>
        <p>One command builds the optimized wasm and the server binary; the next deploys both to Railway or Render. Add auth, storage, jobs, and observability the same way — as you need them.</p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code pp-text="code7"></code></pre>
        <div class="learn-end">
          <a class="cta-primary" href="/docs/getting-started/introduction" pp-route>Read the full docs</a>
          <a class="cta-ghost" href="/components" pp-route>Browse components</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <aside class="learn-preview">
      <div class="learn-preview-card">
        <span class="learn-preview-label">Live preview · <span class="learn-preview-stage" pp-text="stage_note"></span></span>
        <todo-demo :stage="active"></todo-demo>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</root>
